.IX Title "Lucy::Analysis::SnowballStemmer 3pm"
.TH Lucy::Analysis::SnowballStemmer 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Lucy::Analysis::SnowballStemmer \- Reduce related words to a shared root.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 1
\&    my $stemmer = Lucy::Analysis::SnowballStemmer\->new( language => \*(Aqes\*(Aq );
\&    
\&    my $polyanalyzer = Lucy::Analysis::PolyAnalyzer\->new(
\&        analyzers => [ $tokenizer, $normalizer, $stemmer ],
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
This class is a wrapper around the Snowball stemming library, so it supports
the same languages.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
SnowballStemmer is an Analyzer which reduces
related words to a root form (using the “Snowball” stemming library).  For
instance, “horse”, “horses”, and “horsing” all become “hors” – so that a
search for ‘horse’ will also match documents containing ‘horses’ and
‘horsing’.
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.IX Header "CONSTRUCTORS"
.SS new
.IX Subsection "new"
.Vb 1
\&    my $stemmer = Lucy::Analysis::SnowballStemmer\->new( language => \*(Aqes\*(Aq );
.Ve
.PP
Create a new SnowballStemmer.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBlanguage\fR \- A two-letter ISO code identifying a language supported
by Snowball.
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS transform
.IX Subsection "transform"
.Vb 1
\&    my $inversion = $snowball_stemmer\->transform($inversion);
.Ve
.PP
Take a single Inversion as input
and returns an Inversion, either the same one (presumably transformed
in some way), or a new one.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBinversion\fR \- An inversion.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Lucy::Analysis::SnowballStemmer isa Lucy::Analysis::Analyzer isa Clownfish::Obj.
